A063.reason:
Could not break it.

Why the loop always exits through break: line 439 requires committedBatches[b+count] == 0 on entry, and b+count is overflow-checked. revertBatch makes no external call at all (_loadBatchHeader is pure; batchInChallenge is an internal jump), so nothing can re-enter, and the loop body writes only zeros, into committedBatches[b..b+count-1]. When _count reaches 0, _batchIndex == b+count and the hash read there is 0, so the original breaks before it re-tests 'while (_count > 0)'. That condition is therefore false on no execution path. The always-true '_count >= 0' runs exactly the same iterations, and _count never wraps.

Targeted counts, all identical:
- 0 and 1;
- exact span, span+1, span-1 and 10;
- 2^200, 2^255 and MAX-b;
- MAX-1 and MAX, which overflow-revert in both;
- a challenge, or a set revertReqIndex, inside the range.

Random sequences: 895 successful reverts, 515 with count > span (break exit) and 380 with count == span. No difference. The model check also ran the original and the mutant loop on every enabled revert at bounds 4, 6 and 8 and found no difference.
